      "body": "framework_decomposition_weight_percent_observed = 45.58 wt% at 1.013 bar"
    },
    {
      "title": "Mechanism",
      "body": "limited pore opening → uptake"
    },
    {
      "title": "Mechanism",
      "body": "3D framework from 2D inorganic layers linked by Htrz through Cd1 and Cd2 sites → porosity"
    },
    {
      "title": "Design Rule",
      "body": "[positive] use solvothermal assembly with in situ generation/decarboxylation conditions rather than direct ligand mixing → enables formation of complexes 1-5 and single crystals suitable for structure determination, whereas direct or nonsolvothermal routes do not"
    },
    {
      "title": "Design Rule",
      "body": "[positive] select appropriate counteranions during solvothermal synthesis of Cd/Zn triazolate coordination polymers → framework structures and connectivities vary substantially because different anions participate with different coordination modes"
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparison",
      "body": "complex 5 vs previously reported metal/triazolate complexes: winner=subject_a on simultaneous_presence_of_neutral_μ1,2_and_μ2,4_Htrz_bridges"
    }
